leetcode problem 232
AIM:- Implement a first-in-first-out (FIFO) queue using only two stacks. The implemented queue should support all the functions of a normal queue (push, peek, pop, and empty).

ALGORITHM:-
1- Initialize:
A) Two standard stacks, S1 and S2.
2- For push(x) operation:
A) Repeat while S1 is not empty: push the top element of S1 onto S2 and pop it from S1.
B) Push the new element x onto the now-empty S1.
C) Repeat while S2 is not empty: push the top element of S2 back onto S1 and pop it from S2. (This ensures the oldest element is always at the top of S1).
3- For pop() operation:
A) Retrieve the top element of S1 and store it in val.
B) Pop the top element from S1.
C) Return val.
4- For peek() operation:
A) Return the top element of S1 without removing it.
5- For empty() operation:
A) Return true if S1 is empty, otherwise return false.


CODE:-
class MyQueue {
public:
    MyQueue() {
        
    }
    stack<int>S1,S2;
    void push(int x) {
        while(!S1.empty()){
            S2.push(S1.top());
            S1.pop();
        }
        S1.push(x);
        while(!S2.empty()){
            S1.push(S2.top());
            S2.pop();
        }    
    }
    int pop() {
        int val = S1.top();
        S1.pop();
        return val;
    }
    
    int peek() {
        return S1.top();
    }
    
    bool empty() {
        return S1.empty();
    }
};
